  "id": "COMPOUND:18418 - PROTEIN:5781",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Vidalol B may interact with A2780cisR, through a series of target relationships. Vidalol B is implicated as a target in SNU-387, which is a target of Neridienone A and sec-Butyl acetate, (-)-. All these compounds ultimately target A2780cisR. This indicates that Vidalol B may act as a modulator or inhibitor of A2780cisR, possibly through a common pathway involving the downstream targets of SNU-387. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where Vidalol B may influence the biological activity of SNU-387, which in turn affects A2780cisR. The presence of multiple targets and their shared relationship to A2780cisR suggests a possible regulatory or inhibitory role for Vidalol B in the context of this cellular system. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Vidalol B may exert a functional effect on A2780cisR through a mechanism involving the downstream targets of SNU-387.",
